27. Kernel Completion Standard

Kernel 19 is complete when Pantheon has a real, governed bridge to external capability and the bridge has been proven with at least one useful integration.

The goal is not to collect plugins.

The goal is to make Pantheon capable of safely gaining capabilities without weakening Grant’s agency or turning the organism into a pile of special-case integrations.

For email specifically, completion means the architecture needed to retire Terra/Hermes from routine mail ingestion exists and is proven. Do not remove the old path until the replacement has passed its cutover tests.

When complete, report:

files changed
architecture introduced
capability registry schema
approval model
first adapter(s)
mail-intake behavior
attachment allowlist/blocking behavior
tests performed
live evidence
Hermes jobs retired/paused/remaining
known limitations
rollback path
recommended clean predecessor for Kernel 20

Do not begin Kernel 20.